  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t-2)\\,i+\\sqrt{t}\\,j+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,k.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f,$ we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t-2)$ is $t\\in (2,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\sqrt{t}$ is $t\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/assets/33e19c4978f1a0975b6d583f127ff593500d2563acbef5a7cf76b2f6bfaef070.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (2,\\infty ).$",
